            <div xml:id="d62-a2">

                <pb facs="0176" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg76"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pettis to Mr. Medina and Mr. Mendez</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1879-09-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 12,
                    1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, minister resident of the United States of America, has had the
                    honor to receive the note addressed to him which their Excellencies Eulogio D.
                    Medina and Julio Mendez, ministers of the executive council of the republic, did
                    him the honor to write him under date of this day, announcing the sad
                    intelligence of the death of Senor Dr. Pedro J. de Guerra, president of the
                    council and minister of foreign affairs, last night at twelve o’clock, after a
                    sickness of some days, and having previously been apprised of the very
                    unexpected and melancholy event, which the republic of Bolivia has great reason
                    to; and will, deplore. As an evidence of the expression of sorrow which he knows
                    his government will feel, and that the undersigned, does feel, at such a
                    national affliction, he caused the flag of this legation to be placed at
                    half-mast, where it will remain during the day, assuring their excellencies of
                    his own most sincere sympathy in this hour of sorrow, and begs them to accept
                    the assurance of his most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>S. NEWTON PETTIS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
